---
import { comparison } from "../../data/comparison";
import { recentResults } from "../../data/recent-results";
import { snapshot } from "../../data/results";
import { summaryComparisons } from "../../data/supplementary-results";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const { provenance, cohort } = snapshot;
---

<Layout title="Data and reproduction" description="Download the results LegalForecastBench displays and see where they come from.">
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-14 sm:px-6">
		<p class="eyebrow">Data</p>
		<div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-4">
			<h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Data and reproduction</h1>
			<a href="https://github.com/johnhughes3/LegalForecastBench" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-rule-strong px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:border-ink">
				<svg class="size-4" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.013 8.013 0 0016 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"/></svg>
				Source on GitHub
			</a>
		</div>
		<p class="mt-5 text-lg text-ink-2">Download the current combined snapshot and the scored source exports for the six newer agentic configurations. The original beta snapshot remains available.</p>

		<div class="card mt-10 p-6">
			<div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-4">
				<div>
					<h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold">{snapshot.title} · {snapshot.as_of}</h2>
					<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-3">{snapshot.models.length} models · {cohort.case_count} cases · {cohort.unit_count} units</p>
				</div>
				<a href="/data/current.json" download class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-ink px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-bg hover:opacity-90">Download JSON</a>
			</div>
			<dl class="mt-6 grid gap-4 text-sm sm:grid-cols-2">
				<div><dt class="text-ink-3">Release</dt><dd class="mt-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-ink-2">{provenance.release}</dd></div>
				<div><dt class="text-ink-3">Release digest (SHA-256)</dt><dd class="mt-0.5 break-all font-mono text-[13px] text-ink-2">{provenance.release_digest}</dd></div>
			</dl>
			<a class="mt-6 inline-flex text-sm text-accent hover:underline" href="/data/beta-run-mechanics/">Beta Run Mechanics →</a>
		</div>

		<div class="prose-lfb prose mt-12 max-w-none">
			<h2 id="supplementary">Summary-based and minimal-reasoning comparisons</h2>
<p>Three one-shot summary tests, with GPT-4.1 shown separately as a full-record reference. <a href="/experiments/summary-pipelines/#method">Method, provenance, and significance →</a></p>
<ul>{summaryComparisons.map(({source, data}) => <li><a href={`/data/exports/${source.slug}.json`} download>{data.results[0]?.metadata.display_name}</a> · <a href={`https://github.com/johnhughes3/LegalForecastBench/actions/runs/${source.forecast_run}`}>Forecast run</a></li>)}</ul>
<p><a href="/data/summary-comparison/catalog.json" download>Source catalog, archive references, and cost evidence</a> · <a href="https://github.com/johnhughes3/LegalForecastBench/blob/main/docs/site-data.md#summary-comparisons">Reproduction instructions</a></p>
<h2>Source downloads</h2>
            <p><a href="/data/sources.json" download>Run and release provenance for the newer scored exports</a></p>
            <p><a href="/data/beta-2026-09-18.json" download>Historical September 18 beta snapshot</a></p>
            <ul>{recentResults.map(({source, data}) => <li><a href={`/data/exports/${source.slug}.json`} download>{data.results[0]?.metadata.display_name}</a> · <a href={`https://github.com/johnhughes3/LegalForecastBench/actions/runs/${source.forecast_run}`}>Forecast run</a> · <a href={`https://github.com/johnhughes3/LegalForecastBench/actions/runs/${source.scoring_run}`}>Scoring run</a></li>)}</ul>
            <h2 id="significance">Updated significance analysis</h2>
            <p>Paired comparisons for nine configurations. <a href="/data/beta-run-mechanics/#significance">Scope and methodology →</a></p>
            <ul>
                <li><a href="/data/significance/comparison.json" download>Comparison results, confidence intervals, method, and provenance</a></li>
                <li><a href="/data/significance/inputs.json" download>Reproduction input manifest</a></li>
                {comparison.available_models.map(slug=><li><a href={`/data/significance/${slug}.jsonl`} download>{snapshot.models.find(model=>model.slug===slug)?.display_name} public prediction units</a></li>)}
            </ul>
            <p>Download the manifest and all nine JSONL files into the same directory, then run the repository's <a href="https://github.com/johnhughes3/LegalForecastBench/blob/main/scripts/compare_site_results.py">comparison script</a> using the command in the <a href="https://github.com/johnhughes3/LegalForecastBench/blob/main/docs/site-data.md">data contract guide</a>.</p>
            <h2>Reproducing a score</h2>
			<p>The benchmark code, prompts, scorer, and model registries are open source. Official runs execute in GitHub Actions; each model page links its run. Scoring and the exports this site consumes are documented in the repository:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><a href="https://github.com/johnhughes3/LegalForecastBench/blob/main/docs/reproduce-or-audit.md">Reproduce or audit a result</a></li>
				<li><a href="https://github.com/johnhughes3/LegalForecastBench/blob/main/docs/site-data.md">Website data contract</a></li>
				<li><a href="https://github.com/johnhughes3/LegalForecastBench/blob/main/docs/MODEL_RELEASE_DATES.md">Model release dates and training cutoffs</a></li>
			</ul>
			<h2>What is not published</h2>
			<p>Court filings, locked labels, raw model transcripts, and private corpus records are not redistributed here. Model rationales will appear only after human review.</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
